        "original_id": "127d046e-35a9-59b7-ac3d-33e92caa0118",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ellis Ferreira, Boris Becker, Rick Leach, Corina Morariu, Galbraith\n- Events: 2000 Australian Open, 2001 Australian Open, 1997 Stockholm Open – Doubles\n- Roles: professional tennis players, doubles partners\n- Topics: Grand Slam doubles titles, world No. 1 ranking, year-end championships, Masters Series titles, Olympic gold medal\n\nFacts:\n- In 1997, Galbraith partnered Ellis Ferreira in the Stockholm Open doubles event and lost in the final.\n- In 2000, Ellis Ferreira and Rick Leach won the men's doubles title at the Australian Open.\n- In 2001, Ellis Ferreira and Corina Morariu won the mixed doubles title at the Australian Open.\n- Ellis Ferreira won two Grand Slam doubles titles.\n- Boris Franz Becker, born on 22 November 1967, is a German former professional tennis player who reached world No. 1.\n- Boris Becker won five year-end championships, 13 Masters Series titles, and an Olympic gold medal in doubles.",
